SQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Conservation services forecasting \u00a30.28m overspend for maintaining public green spaces and meeting management responsibilities.","detail":"A relatively small area of overspend (Conservation within Transport & Environment) is driven by costs of maintaining publicly accessible green spaces and meeting statutory management responsibilities. This is presented as an unavoidable cost rather than a control issue.","category":"overspend","matters":"A service area where costs are driven by statutory obligations and cannot be reduced without changing the scope of service; signals inflexibility in budget structure.","figures":"\u00a30.28m overspend in Conservation","quote":"Conservation: A \u00a30.28m overspend is forecast, reflecting the cost of keeping publicly accessible green spaces safe and meeting the Council's management responsibilities.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Category 2 highway defects repaired within 28 days at 73.2%, significantly below 90% target, driven by historic underinvestment and increased network deterioration.","detail":"Highway repair performance is 16.8 percentage points below target. The report attributes this to a severe winter, historic underinvestment that has increased network deterioration, and stretched operational capacity. The council expects improvement in Q2 as weather improves and additional investment begins to take effect.","category":"capital","matters":"Persistent underperformance on routine highways maintenance suggests a capital backlog that has not been addressed; this indicates either deferred spending or insufficient capital investment, both of which indicate financial stress on the council's infrastructure position.","figures":"73.2% of Category 2 defects repaired within 28 days vs 90% target","quote":"Performance remains under pressure following a severe winter and the continuing impact of historic underinvestment, which has increased network deterioration and stretched operational capacity.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Baums Lane/A60 scheme cost estimates likely to exceed original budget; additional external funding being sought.","detail":"A capital highways scheme is running over budget. The council is attempting to secure additional funding from EMCCA (East Midlands Combined County Authority) but the outcome is not confirmed. Implementation is planned for January 2027.","category":"capital","matters":"A capital scheme in overspend that requires external funding to proceed signals the council's own capital capacity is exhausted and it is dependent on external sources for core infrastructure; this matters for forward planning and debt capacity.","figures":"Budget shortfall amount not stated; implementation January 2027","quote":"Current cost estimates are likely to exceed the original budget. Additional EMCCA funding is being sought, with implementation currently planned for January 2027.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Property Safety and Facilities Management forecasting \u00a30.48m overspend, with \u00a30.75m savings target under pressure from utility and maintenance costs.","detail":"The portfolio is running \u00a30.48m over budget at mid-year. The budget already contained a \u00a30.75m savings requirement that the council is trying to implement, but higher maintenance and utility costs are creating additional pressure. Some offset is expected from future income.","category":"overspend","matters":"A service area where savings targets are competing with unavoidable cost pressures signals either a real structural shortfall or that the savings programme is at risk; this directly affects the council's financial sustainability.","figures":"\u00a30.48m overspend, \u00a30.75m savings requirement in 2026/27 budget","quote":"Property Safety and Facilities Management is forecasting a \u00a30.48m overspend. The 2026/27 budget includes a \u00a30.75m savings requirement, and measures are being implemented to address this. However, higher maintenance and utility costs are creating additional pressure.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Place Department forecasting \u00a30.861m net revenue overspend for 2026/27 after use of reserves.","detail":"The department's forecast position shows a \u00a30.861m overspend across three portfolio areas. This is after planned use of reserves, indicating the underlying pressure is larger than the reported figure.","category":"overspend","matters":"Mid-year overspend forecasts signal budget management issues that will need either in-year reduction or reserve draw; a lender needs to know if the council is managing to its budget.","figures":"\u00a30.861m net revenue overspend forecast for 2026/27","quote":"At Period 4, the Place Department (excluding Public Health) is forecasting a net revenue overspend of \u00a30.861m for 2026/27, after the planned use of reserves.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Nottinghamshire CC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Conservation services forecasting \u00a30.28m overspend for maintaining public green spaces and meeting management responsibilities.","lead":"A service area where costs are driven by statutory obligations and cannot be reduced without changing the scope of service; signals inflexibility in budget structure.","also":["14 other findings in this window"],"watch":null,"n_findings":15,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Place Department Performance - Quarter 1 2026-27","top_paper_url":"https://www.nottinghamshire.gov.uk/DMS/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=p8ApBomc3O0hOw68J5g7abt3QeYbsaTb6cQ%2bpFJvVZDGiJHVoPUnFA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","draft":true},"findings_t